#import "/_lib/0.1.1.typ": *
#show: template

#taxon[Definition]
#title[Symmetries of a pointed Type]

Given a pointed type $X -= (A,a)$, we define $Omega X :-= (a =_A a)$. We call
points in $Omega X$ the symmetries of $a : A$.
Notice that the type $Omega X$ is pointed at $"refl"_a$.
See #link("00D6")[Symmetry Book, Definition 4.2.10]
